@@ -2217,6 +2217,18 @@ The exceeded limits can be [monitored](#monitoring) with the following metrics:
 
 These limits are approximate, so VictoriaMetrics can underflow/overflow the limit by a small percentage (usually less than 1%).
 
+While the metrics above show the aggregate number of dropped samples, they don't show which metric names are responsible for it.
+This information can be obtained via the `/internal/series_limit_exceeded` HTTP endpoint, which returns metric names with the highest
+number of samples dropped because of `-storage.maxHourlySeries` or `-storage.maxDailySeries` being exceeded, since the last reset:
+
+```sh
+curl http://localhost:8428/internal/series_limit_exceeded?limit=10
+```
+
+The counters can be reset via the `/internal/series_limit_exceeded/reset` endpoint. This tracking is enabled by default and can be disabled
+via `-storage.trackSeriesLimitExceededMetricNames=false`. The memory it uses is bounded and can be configured via
